<<<P5
// --- agent-mesh pairwise peer auth (F5). Peers can't verify each other's aga_ tokens
// (only the hub holds connect_token_hash, 1413). Hub is the trust root: it mints a
// short-lived opaque ticket and pushes the expectation to the callee. NO new crypto. ---
// Wire (new WS actions, added beside the agent_capabilities_sync route):
//   Daemon A -> hub:   { action:'peer_ticket_request', targetAgentId }
//   Hub -> Daemon A:   { type:'peer_ticket', ticket, exp, peer:{ agentId, addrs:[{host,port,scope}] } }
//   Hub -> Daemon B:   { type:'peer_ticket_grant', ticket, exp, fromAgentId }   (push on B's hub ws)
//   Daemon A -> B (FIRST frame on B's LAN listener ws): { type:'peer_auth', ticket, fromAgentId }
//   Daemon B: match ticket + fromAgentId + now<exp against the grant it holds; else close(1008).
// Mint: ticket = `agp_${crypto.randomBytes(24).toString('base64url')}` (like createAgentConnectToken,1204).
// Hub guards on peer_ticket_request: A authed (ws.agentAuth); B live in the SAME workspace
// (findConnectedAgent,1628); B's stored capabilities.reach.listening === true. Otherwise reject.
// Hub holds pendingPeerTickets Map<ticket,{from,to,exp}>, single-use, TTL ~60s, swept like
// mcpAgentPresence(1516). The callee validates the presented ticket against its received grant —
// hub-verified indirectly, so B needs no server secret.
>>>
PLAN P6<-F6 op=insert at=agent/agensis-cli/src/agensis.mjs:672-673#"async function pushCapabilitiesSnapshot(ws, config) {" why=no-listener ref=agent/agensis-cli/src/agensis.mjs:73-84,153-156,645,656-667 test="node --test tests/agent-mesh.test.cjs" order=3 fill=-
<<<P6
// F6 daemon LAN listener — OPT-IN, DEFAULT OFF (Q2). Enable via config.lanListener
// (--lan flag / AGENSIS_LAN=1). When enabled: open a ws WebSocket.Server on port 0
// (OS-assigned ephemeral), bound to the LAN interface; every inbound socket MUST send the
// F5 { type:'peer_auth', ticket, fromAgentId } first frame (validate vs peer_ticket_grant).
// Build reach from the bound port + os.networkInterfaces() IPv4 (internal===false):
//   reach = { transport:'ws', listening:true,  addrs:[{host,port,scope:'lan'}], auth:'hub-pairwise' }
// When OFF or after kill-switch:
//   reach = { transport:'ws', listening:false, addrs:[],                        auth:'hub-pairwise' }
// Send `reach` inside pushCapabilitiesSnapshot's send({action:'agent_capabilities_sync',...},656)
// AND fold JSON.stringify(reach) into capabilitiesHash in computeCapabilities(645) so a reach
// change re-pushes over the existing agent_capabilities_refresh drift nudge — no 2nd channel.
// Hub kill-switch: server pushes { type:'agent_reach_disable' }; daemon handles it beside
// agent_capabilities_refresh(153): close the listener, then pushCapabilitiesSnapshot with
// listening:false. Hub may push this regardless of the daemon's opt-in (Q2).
>>>
